  "notes": "Loanword from English 'curve'. Used both for shapes/lines in everyday speech and as a baseball term.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {急|きゅう}カーブ: sharp curve\n- カーブを{曲|ま}がる: to go around a curve\n- カーブする: to curve (verb form)\n- カーブミラー: convex mirror at road curves\n- {学習|がくしゅう}カーブ: learning curve\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {曲線|きょくせん}: curve (mathematical/abstract) — more formal, used for geometric curves\n- カーブ: everyday curves of roads, graphs, or pitches; also functions as a する verb",
